WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.169 --> 00:00:03.086
(mysterious music)

00:00:08.990 --> 00:00:11.323
(footsteps)

00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:15.414
(buzzing)

00:00:20.077 --> 00:00:22.393
- [Interviewer] Do you experience any PTSD

00:00:22.393 --> 00:00:25.257
from your time at the CIA?

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:27.477
- I have nightmares, sure.

00:00:27.477 --> 00:00:28.394
Flashbacks.

00:00:32.425 --> 00:00:33.951
- So how did that translate into the work

00:00:33.951 --> 00:00:35.078
you're actually doing?

00:00:35.078 --> 00:00:37.861
- I can't talk about
operational work, so--

00:00:37.861 --> 00:00:40.478
I don't think it really,

00:00:40.478 --> 00:00:41.712
I don't think there's
really a way to answer

00:00:41.712 --> 00:00:44.627
that without talking about shifting from

00:00:44.627 --> 00:00:45.981
this kind of work to that kind of work,

00:00:45.981 --> 00:00:47.981
do you know what I mean?

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.337
- Are there things you can talk about?

00:00:58.502 --> 00:01:00.492
- When you leave the agency you go through

00:01:00.492 --> 00:01:04.155
a long process of having
your cover rolled back.

00:01:04.155 --> 00:01:07.988
And I'm able to talk
about having worked there

00:01:09.247 --> 00:01:11.939
but obviously not the details of any

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:13.689
particular operation.

00:01:20.957 --> 00:01:22.962
(footsteps)

00:01:22.962 --> 00:01:27.129
(city noises)
(mysterious music)

00:01:28.375 --> 00:01:31.105
In my early twenties
I created an algorithm

00:01:31.105 --> 00:01:34.842
to predict areas in the world that would

00:01:34.842 --> 00:01:37.509
give rise to terrorist activity.

00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:42.217
I wanted to deconstruct what it is

00:01:42.217 --> 00:01:44.134
that creates terrorism.

00:01:53.258 --> 00:01:54.885
Spending years in another
country where nobody

00:01:54.885 --> 00:01:56.590
knows what you do or who you really are

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.423
is lonely.

00:01:58.344 --> 00:02:01.594
I mean it's lonely in the small moments

00:02:02.692 --> 00:02:05.525
really as much as the big moments.

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:10.052
You can't really have honest or frank

00:02:10.052 --> 00:02:12.976
conversation even in your own home.

00:02:12.976 --> 00:02:16.947
Because of surveillance
and being listened to

00:02:16.947 --> 00:02:17.947
and watched.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.170
(waves crashing)

00:02:37.317 --> 00:02:39.650
(exploding)

00:02:41.199 --> 00:02:44.595
I did see things that I'll
never be able to un-see.

00:02:44.595 --> 00:02:49.084
(urgent talking in foreign language)

00:02:49.084 --> 00:02:53.001
Humans not seeing the
humanity in other humans.

00:02:54.119 --> 00:02:57.063
(urgent talking in foreign language)

00:02:57.063 --> 00:02:59.319
(gunshots)

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:02.991
Whether that's torture
or killings that are

00:03:02.991 --> 00:03:05.561
undertaken with the
same kind of callousness

00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:08.040
as a butcher might take
to a piece of meat.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:10.790
(waves crashing)

00:03:14.205 --> 00:03:16.705
(light music)

00:03:18.258 --> 00:03:20.425
Is there a coyote in here?

00:03:23.527 --> 00:03:25.097
You have snuggy dreams?

00:03:25.097 --> 00:03:25.930
- Yeah.

00:03:27.002 --> 00:03:28.472
(giggling)

00:03:28.472 --> 00:03:29.761
- Wanna get some breakfast?

00:03:29.761 --> 00:03:30.594
- Okay.

00:03:30.594 --> 00:03:32.011
- Okay, let's go.

00:03:40.684 --> 00:03:41.767
There you go.

00:03:48.122 --> 00:03:51.722
As a parent, is my greatest responsibility

00:03:51.722 --> 00:03:55.055
to go out and make the world a more safe

00:03:57.787 --> 00:04:00.795
and peaceful place for
my daughter to inherit.

00:04:00.795 --> 00:04:03.907
Or is it to be at home snug with her

00:04:03.907 --> 00:04:06.785
reading Harry Potter and the world

00:04:06.785 --> 00:04:08.702
she inherits be damned.

00:04:16.064 --> 00:04:17.648
Hey, John, it's Amaryllis.

00:04:17.648 --> 00:04:19.243
Were you able to get the Kurdish authority

00:04:19.243 --> 00:04:22.863
on the phone about the date change?

00:04:22.863 --> 00:04:24.304
I'm a little worried

00:04:24.304 --> 00:04:26.197
with all the build up around Mosul.

00:04:26.197 --> 00:04:27.613
I wanna make sure we're de-conflicting

00:04:27.613 --> 00:04:29.373
with the Iraqi military.

00:04:29.373 --> 00:04:31.003
Yeah, try DC and give me a ring back.

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:31.836
Okay.

00:04:35.298 --> 00:04:36.908
I've created an organization called

00:04:36.908 --> 00:04:38.221
Operation Zoë.

00:04:38.221 --> 00:04:39.584
Zoë meaning life and also being

00:04:39.584 --> 00:04:41.167
my daughter's name.

00:04:42.017 --> 00:04:44.737
I wanted to take former military officers

00:04:44.737 --> 00:04:46.569
and intelligence officers
who've all learned

00:04:46.569 --> 00:04:49.230
very specialized skills
in order to wage war

00:04:49.230 --> 00:04:52.687
and allow them to use
those specialized skills

00:04:52.687 --> 00:04:54.604
in order to wage peace.

00:04:55.674 --> 00:04:57.983
George, hi, my friend.

00:04:57.983 --> 00:05:00.441
I would love to see you.

00:05:00.441 --> 00:05:02.459
Nobody's Kurdish is like your Kurdish.

00:05:02.459 --> 00:05:03.775
I think we're gonna have at least a night

00:05:03.775 --> 00:05:05.307
in Erbil and we'll stay at the Rotana

00:05:05.307 --> 00:05:07.805
'cause their security is amazing

00:05:07.805 --> 00:05:11.996
and their security team
is trained by US Forces.

00:05:11.996 --> 00:05:13.522
They've got double blast walls,

00:05:13.522 --> 00:05:14.798
snipers on the roof,

00:05:14.798 --> 00:05:16.642
so I feel pretty good about that.

00:05:16.642 --> 00:05:18.809
But you could meet us there.

00:05:20.064 --> 00:05:23.273
(speaking foreign language)

00:05:23.273 --> 00:05:24.394
I think one of the greatest lessons

00:05:24.394 --> 00:05:27.664
that I took away from
my career at the agency

00:05:27.664 --> 00:05:31.664
is this underlying truth
that everybody believes

00:05:34.212 --> 00:05:35.813
they are the good guy.

00:05:35.813 --> 00:05:38.591
And for many people in Syria and Iraq

00:05:38.591 --> 00:05:41.064
and Pakistan and Yemen and Somalia

00:05:41.064 --> 00:05:44.737
and other places where
we're flying drones.

00:05:44.737 --> 00:05:47.987
The idea of being kept safe by American

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.437
sky robots that kill people without

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:59.655
making a sound is as upsetting and driving

00:06:00.866 --> 00:06:04.448
as much desire for conflict
in the Islamic world

00:06:04.448 --> 00:06:07.768
as the atrocities that
we see Isis committing

00:06:07.768 --> 00:06:10.518
is driving in the American world.

00:06:13.483 --> 00:06:17.650
(birds chirping)
(footsteps)

00:06:21.556 --> 00:06:24.761
(speaking foreign language)

00:06:24.761 --> 00:06:25.723
Do you know what (foreign language) means?

00:06:25.723 --> 00:06:26.556
- [Zoë] What?

00:06:26.556 --> 00:06:28.223
- Heaven or the sky.

00:06:31.038 --> 00:06:34.893
I travel so frequently
but it's never routine.

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:36.650
It's the minute that you find it routine

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:38.274
that you stop being aware and stop

00:06:38.274 --> 00:06:42.600
taking precautions when
you're on the ground.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:43.585
And you're gonna have
the most amazing week.

00:06:43.585 --> 00:06:45.776
And I will see you when I get home.

00:06:45.776 --> 00:06:48.111
I love you so, so, so, so much.

00:06:48.111 --> 00:06:48.944
- Bye.

00:06:48.944 --> 00:06:49.777
- I'll talk to you tonight.

00:06:49.777 --> 00:06:50.610
- Okay.

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:51.860
- Bye, my love.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:57.563
Bye.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:03.070
(waves crashing)

00:07:09.933 --> 00:07:12.573
(slow music)

00:07:12.573 --> 00:07:14.156
My sweetest coyote,

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:17.459
More than anything, I
wish I could hold you

00:07:17.459 --> 00:07:19.555
as you read this.

00:07:19.555 --> 00:07:22.146
Wish I could wrap you up in my arms

00:07:22.146 --> 00:07:23.857
and tell you how you're my best friend

00:07:23.857 --> 00:07:25.440
and wisest teacher.

00:07:28.877 --> 00:07:31.507
I wish I could read you
this snugged in our bed

00:07:31.507 --> 00:07:33.886
with the world at bay outside our window

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.886
and only love around us.

00:07:37.511 --> 00:07:41.150
But I'm writing you this
letter in case I can't.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:45.562
In case I've been stopped
or hurt or killed.

00:07:45.562 --> 00:07:49.487
In case it's only my love and not my arms

00:07:49.487 --> 00:07:51.320
that hold you tonight.

00:07:55.271 --> 00:07:57.380
(intense music)

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:59.630
(gunshots)

00:08:00.983 --> 00:08:03.150
(yelling)

00:08:06.117 --> 00:08:10.284
(radio static)
- [Officer] Engage, engage.

00:08:11.583 --> 00:08:15.500
(speaking in foreign language)

00:08:16.581 --> 00:08:19.414
(heavy breathing)

00:08:23.382 --> 00:08:26.747
I want to explain why
I've put myself in danger.

00:08:26.747 --> 00:08:29.672
Why I've risked a lifetime
of telling stories

00:08:29.672 --> 00:08:32.039
with you in the park.

00:08:32.039 --> 00:08:35.241
As you grew deep beneath my navel,

00:08:35.241 --> 00:08:38.074
I felt all of humanity inside you.

00:08:39.598 --> 00:08:43.205
The truth is all over
this tiny speck in space.

00:08:43.205 --> 00:08:45.088
We humans are the same.

00:08:45.088 --> 00:08:48.174
Craving of love, of understanding,

00:08:48.174 --> 00:08:50.174
of being heard and seen.

00:08:59.025 --> 00:08:59.858
Can we just go to

00:08:59.858 --> 00:09:02.775
SFO International Terminal, please?

00:09:12.793 --> 00:09:15.376
(wind blowing)

00:09:17.173 --> 00:09:19.923
Things can change in a heartbeat.

00:09:21.278 --> 00:09:25.409
You don't know who is
manning the checkpoint.

00:09:25.409 --> 00:09:26.385
In some cases they are manned by

00:09:26.385 --> 00:09:28.118
the Iraqi military and other cases by

00:09:28.118 --> 00:09:31.716
extremist groups who
are operating locally.

00:09:31.716 --> 00:09:33.133
Checkpoint Three.

00:09:35.432 --> 00:09:36.615
(speaking foreign language)

00:09:36.615 --> 00:09:38.203
- [Passenger] Yes, I have my passport.

00:09:38.203 --> 00:09:41.782
- Mine's in the trunk,
can we open the trunk?

00:09:41.782 --> 00:09:43.051
Oh, I stay here?

00:09:43.051 --> 00:09:44.512
(speaking foreign language)

00:09:44.512 --> 00:09:46.345
Okay, we'll pull over.

00:09:52.756 --> 00:09:55.098
He's speaking in Kurdish.

00:09:55.098 --> 00:09:58.265
We'll get out and grab our ID for him.

00:10:13.262 --> 00:10:16.262
(mysterious noises)

00:10:20.802 --> 00:10:23.302
(light music)

00:10:25.185 --> 00:10:26.930
The aim of this trip is to spend time

00:10:26.930 --> 00:10:30.116
with Syrian and Iraqi
young people who have

00:10:30.116 --> 00:10:32.114
all lost family to the fighting and have

00:10:32.114 --> 00:10:34.953
put together reconciliation programs to

00:10:34.953 --> 00:10:37.870
build trust with one another again.

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.917
(speaking foreign language)

00:10:49.906 --> 00:10:52.556
To be in the energy of
these kids who've seen

00:10:52.556 --> 00:10:56.315
such savagery and just so much passion

00:10:56.315 --> 00:10:59.371
and intellectual
curiosity about what it is

00:10:59.371 --> 00:11:02.011
they can do to make sure that this doesn't

00:11:02.011 --> 00:11:04.227
happen again on their watch.

00:11:04.227 --> 00:11:05.381
At least in their country,

00:11:05.381 --> 00:11:06.956
at least for their generation.

00:11:06.956 --> 00:11:09.857
They are committed to peace.

00:11:09.857 --> 00:11:12.607
(waves crashing)

00:11:19.628 --> 00:11:22.878
We're ten years plus into one narrative

00:11:24.970 --> 00:11:26.921
about the war on terrorism.

00:11:26.921 --> 00:11:28.671
And it's very binary.

00:11:30.561 --> 00:11:33.350
What we're doing is not bringing an end

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:34.767
to this conflict.

00:11:42.571 --> 00:11:43.957
Ever since I was little I've really loved

00:11:43.957 --> 00:11:45.207
this Rumi poem.

00:11:46.711 --> 00:11:49.819
Out beyond ideas of
wrongdoing and right doing.

00:11:49.819 --> 00:11:51.119
There is a field.

00:11:51.119 --> 00:11:53.316
I'll meet you there.

00:11:53.316 --> 00:11:54.900
(light music)

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:56.915
I love that idea,

00:11:56.915 --> 00:12:00.112
because the more that
I was out in the field,

00:12:00.112 --> 00:12:02.601
the more I realized that
the question is almost

00:12:02.601 --> 00:12:05.413
always not who is right and who is wrong.

00:12:05.413 --> 00:12:09.729
Almost always both sides
are partially right

00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:12.033
and it's important for us to be able

00:12:12.033 --> 00:12:14.725
to put ourselves in our adversaries shoes

00:12:14.725 --> 00:12:17.691
and invite them to put
themselves in our shoes

00:12:17.691 --> 00:12:19.837
so that we understand what is driving

00:12:19.837 --> 00:12:22.837
this conflict or it goes on forever.

00:12:27.427 --> 00:12:29.927
(light music)

00:12:33.708 --> 00:12:34.805
Every single person that you meet

00:12:34.805 --> 00:12:36.811
is made out of star stuff.

00:12:36.811 --> 00:12:38.061
And so are you.

00:12:42.051 --> 00:12:45.179
- What a beautiful night it is.

00:12:45.179 --> 00:12:48.512
With the stars up in the dark night sky.

00:12:49.753 --> 00:12:52.615
All the people turning out the lights

00:12:52.615 --> 00:12:54.115
and settling down.

00:12:56.297 --> 00:12:59.714
All flowers tucked under the dirt asleep.

00:13:01.854 --> 00:13:04.723
The city is going to sleep.

00:13:04.723 --> 00:13:07.140
What a beautiful night it is.

00:13:33.468 --> 00:13:36.261
- I'm with you now as you read this.

00:13:36.261 --> 00:13:38.511
And always in every breath.

00:13:41.913 --> 00:13:44.136
Do not fear the darkness.

00:13:44.136 --> 00:13:47.258
You have in your heart
the brightest of lanterns.

00:13:47.258 --> 00:13:49.742
Let your love fill you with warmth,

00:13:49.742 --> 00:13:51.813
that you might fill others,

00:13:51.813 --> 00:13:53.659
and they still others,

00:13:53.659 --> 00:13:56.909
until the world is lit from your heart.

00:14:00.783 --> 00:14:02.659
You are the love of my life.

00:14:02.659 --> 00:14:03.576
Your momma.

00:14:17.236 --> 00:14:20.153
(mysterious music)

00:14:38.182 --> 00:14:40.682
(light music)

